abstract: "Replication code and derived-data aggregates for a study comparing idiosyncratic volatility estimates between a current-constituent S&P 500 panel and a delisting-inclusive full-universe panel constructed from Sharadar SF1. The two panels differ significantly under a matched convention, but the corrected panel's own estimate is an imprecise near-zero rather than a confirmed zero, and a survival-conditioning ladder initially read as independent confirmation of the survivorship mechanism is shown to be predominantly a birth-cohort artifact. Raw third-party fundamental data (Sharadar SF1) are not redistributed; see README for data-access terms."
